following_english_context:
and there is a riuer in the countrey of Mauritania which hath the same name, of which it is most manifest that diuers Greeke Histories make mention, as also of the countrey neere adioyning, which they call the countrey of Phut, but it hath chaunged his present name by the meanes of one Libis one of the sonnes of Misraim; (but why it is called Africa, I will heareafter signifie  vnto you). As touching Canaan the fourth sonne of Cham, he dwelled in the countrey at this day called Iudaea, and called it the countrey of Canaan according to his name. They also had children:

for Chus had sixe, amongst whom Sabas established the Sabians, and Euilas the Euileans,  
